1
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,750
Oh, hey, Joey.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,750
Mmm.

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:08,090
Hey.

4
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:08,090
Listen, I need to ask you something.

5
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,130
You know how my stepdad's in prison?

6
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,380
Yeah.

7
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,380
Yeah.

8
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:16,590
He was supposed to get a weekend furlough so he could go to the wedding.

9
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,930
But he just called and...

10
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:24,100
Well, apparently stabbing Iceman in the exercise yard couldn't wait till Monday.

11
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,560
So he can't come?

12
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,560
No.

13
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:29,980
And so there's no one to walk me down the aisle. And...

14
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:33,610
Well, I would just really love it if you would do it.

15
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,320
Seriously?

16
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,320
Yeah.

17
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:39,240
You've, you know, sort of been like a dad to me.

18
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:44,460
You've always, you know, looked out for me and shared your wisdom.

19
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,460
I am pretty "wisdomous."

20
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:52,960
So, what do you say?

21
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:56,800
Are you kidding? Phoebe, I would be honored.

22
00:00:57,590 --> 00:00:59,800
PHOEBE: Oh, thank you.

23
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,720
I hope...

24
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:06,480
I hope you know how much you mean to me.

25
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,150
Listen, I hope...

26
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,650
I hope that you know...

27
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:17,490
I don't want you to see your father cry. Go to your room!

28
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:11,540
Oh.

29
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:11,540
Oh, no, no, no. Let your dad get this.

30
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:19,720
Oh. It's my wedding planner. She's driving me crazy!

31
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:24,600
Hello? Okay, stop screaming!

32
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,390
Okay, so halibut.

33
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,230
All right, so salmon. Either way. I don't...

34
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,150
It doesn't matter to me.

35
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,150
Well, it matters to me!

36
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:38,190
Well, I don't care. So you pick.

37
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,490
Did you just hang up on me?

38
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:45,120
All right, look, I need you at the rehearsal dinner tonight at 1800 hours.

39
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,450
Okay. What time is that?

40
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:50,580
You don't know military time?

41
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:53,960
I must have been in missile training the day they taught that.

42
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,710
Just subtract 12.

43
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,460
Okay, so 1800 minus 12...

44
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:02,090
...is 1788.

45
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,300
Six o'clock!

46
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,300
Okay.

47
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,220
Hold on. Yeah? Geller here.

48
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:11,190
No, I said it has to be there by 4:00. Goodbye.

49
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:13,690
How hard is it to make an ice sculpture?

50
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,480
That sounds really fancy.

51
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:18,030
I told you, I just want a simple wedding.

52
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:20,900
Please, honey, leave the details to me.

53
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:23,780
Now, I wanna make this day as special for you as I can.

54
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:26,160
I was thinking the harpist should wear white.

55
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:29,620
Harpist? My friend Marjorie is playing the steel drums.

56
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:32,620
Oh, she backed out.

57
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:32,620
She did? Why?

58
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:34,630
I made her.

59
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:37,040
Steel drums don't really say "elegant wedding."

60
00:03:37,210 --> 00:03:40,630
Nor does Marjorie's overwhelming scent.

61
00:03:37,210 --> 00:03:40,630
Hey!

62
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,880
She will shower when Tibet is free.

63
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:56,270
Hey. You look great.

64
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:56,270
You too.

65
00:03:56,440 --> 00:04:01,530
I'm glad we're having a rehearsal dinner. I rarely practice my meals before I eat.

66
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,660
What did we say was your one gift to us?

67
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:08,330
No stupid jokes, but I thought that was for the actual wedding.

68
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:10,330
Rehearse it.

69
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,450
Hi.

70
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,830
Thanks for coming, you guys.

71
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,830
Oh, yeah...

72
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:18,500
I was... I was going for a handshake.

73
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:20,500
That why your hand's against my crotch?

74
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:22,760
That is why.

75
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:22,760
Yeah.

76
00:04:24,050 --> 00:04:26,090
So, Rach, where's Emma?

77
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,970
Monica made me send her to my mom's.

78
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:31,010
Apparently, babies and weddings don't mix.

79
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:34,350
Are you still crying about your damn baby?

80
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:39,020
Pheebs, you got to keep the line moving. Remember, 20 seconds per person.

81
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:40,980
You see these clowns all the time.

82
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:47,700
Hey, you're Mike's parents, right?

83
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:47,700
Yes, we are.

84
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:50,700
Gosh, our little ones are growing up fast, aren't they?

85
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,700
How's that?

86
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,700
You know...

87
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:57,370
...on one hand, you're happy for them. On the other, it's hard to let go.

88
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,960
Who in God's name are you?

89
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:05,720
I'm not that fond of you either, buddy. I'm just trying to be nice for the kids.

90
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:12,680
You know what? We have no idea what we're doing in the wedding tomorrow.

91
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:15,730
I thought we'd be groomsmen. They would have asked us by now.

92
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:18,400
When did they ask you to be a bridesmaid?

93
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:22,730
November.

94
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:22,730
I wanna say it's not looking good.

95
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:24,900
Hey, Pheebs?

96
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:24,900
Huh?

97
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:28,700
You haven't told these guys what they're doing in the wedding yet.

98
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:31,410
Um, well, they're not in the wedding.

99
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,240
What?

100
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,870
Well...

101
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:41,590
...this is really awkward.

102
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:44,420
Oh, and I can leave.

103
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:49,930
I'm sorry, you guys. But Mike's got his brother and his friends from school.

104
00:05:50,090 --> 00:05:52,100
So, you know, you were...

105
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:56,680
If it helps, you were next in line. You just missed the cut.

106
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:58,230
Oh, man.

107
00:05:58,390 --> 00:06:01,650
This is like figure skating team all over again.

108
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:06,570
I mean, synchronized swimming.

109
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,740
I mean... I mean, the balance beam.

110
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:11,240
Help me.

111
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:11,240
Football.

112
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:13,030
Thank you.

113
00:06:13,530 --> 00:06:15,910
Oh, Pheebs, spit that out. That has pork in it.

114
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,450
Oh! Oh!

115
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:20,540
I thought the pot stickers were supposed to be vegetarian?

116
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:23,630
Yeah, I changed them. I sent you a fax about it.

117
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,170
I don't have a fax machine.

118
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:29,970
Huh. Well, then there are gonna be a few surprises.

119
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:35,430
I can't believe we're gonna be the only people not in the wedding.

120
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,140
I know. I hate being left out of things.

121
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:39,140
And it's a wedding.

122
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:42,060
It'll be weird if I'm not in it.

123
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:46,150
Hey, guys, how's it going?

124
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:46,150
Fine.

125
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:51,200
We're sitting here, alone, doing nothing. It's our rehearsal for tomorrow.

126
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:54,280
Look, about tomorrow, I've got a question for you.

127
00:06:54,450 --> 00:06:57,660
I found out one of my groomsmen had an emergency and can't make it.

128
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:00,500
What happened?

129
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:00,500
Who cares? And?

130
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:03,790
And I was wondering if one of you guys...

131
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,210
I'll do it!

132
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,210
Me!

133
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,510
You both wanna do it? There's only room for one.

134
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,340
Pick me. I look great in a tux, and I won't steal focus.

135
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:17,010
No, Mike. No, no, you wanna pick me. I mean... Watch.

136
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,850
Huh?

137
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:25,650
You know, I really don't feel very comfortable making this decision.

138
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:28,980
You know, Phoebe knows you better. I'm gonna let her choose.

139
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:35,200
Well, if Phoebe's choosing, then say hello to Mike's next groomsman.

140
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,660
Oh, I will. But I will need a mirror...

141
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,870
...as he is me.

142
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,630
Please. You're going down.

143
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,630
You are going "downer."

144
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:47,710
They say that on the figure skating team?

145
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:50,630
I wouldn't know. I didn't make it.

146
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:56,510
You know I'm filling in for Phoebe's stepdad tomorrow, right?

147
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:00,220
Yeah. Yeah. Hey, thanks for doing that.

148
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:00,220
Oh, hey, my pleasure.

149
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,020
So, what are your intentions with my Phoebe?

150
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:07,560
I intend to marry her.

151
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:07,560
Oh, a wiseacre.

152
00:08:09,570 --> 00:08:13,700
I understand you plan to support your wife by playing the piano?

153
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,410
Isn't that kind of unstable?

154
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,490
No more so than acting.

155
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,490
Strike two.

156
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:23,910
You're right. She probably will support me.

157
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,330
Hey, unless we move in with you, Dad.

158
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,590
Strike three.

159
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,090
You only get one more, Mike.

160
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:38,010
So? What did you decide?

161
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,720
I decided to pee.

162
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,390
You have to choose one of us to be in your wedding.

163
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,940
One of the groomsmen fell out.

164
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,940
Oh, no, no.

165
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:50,730
I can't choose between you two. I love you both so much.

166
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:54,570
Just not enough to put us in the original wedding party.

167
00:08:55,070 --> 00:08:57,450
But I don't wanna choose. It's...

168
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,570
Okay, wait. Rach?

169
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,570
Yeah?

170
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:03,120
Listen, I have a very special bridesmaid task for you to do.

171
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:05,250
Goody! What is it?

172
00:09:05,410 --> 00:09:07,790
Well, there's a spot open for only one groomsman...

173
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:11,630
...and you have to choose between Ross and Chandler. So good luck with that.

174
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:14,550
What? What, what, what? No, I don't wanna do that.

175
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,630
I guess I have to find a new bridesmaid.

176
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,550
I'll do it!

177
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,800
Okay, it's 2100 hours.

178
00:09:20,970 --> 00:09:23,890
Time for your toast.

179
00:09:20,970 --> 00:09:23,890
Do I have time to go to the bathroom?

180
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:28,350
You had a bathroom break at 2030. Pee on your own time, Mike.

181
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,400
In regards to the toasts, okay, you wanna keep them short.

182
00:09:33,570 --> 00:09:36,570
Nothing kills a rehearsal dinner like long speeches. Okay.

183
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:39,070
You just get in, do your thing, and get out.

184
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,990
Is that what you say to Chandler?

185
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:45,500
It's 2101, and I am not amused.

186
00:09:46,870 --> 00:09:48,460
Okay.

187
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:52,630
The bride and groom have a few words they'd like to say.

188
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:56,630
Okay. Hello, everyone.

189
00:09:56,800 --> 00:10:00,930
And thank you all for being here tonight. So tomorrow's the big event.

190
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:05,270
Some of you might not know, but Mike and I didn't get off to the best start.

191
00:10:05,470 --> 00:10:08,810
Yeah. My friend Joey and I...

192
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:13,360
...decided to fix each other up with friends. So I...

193
00:10:15,690 --> 00:10:18,190
Oh, okay. I...

194
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,530
I thought about it, and I fixed him up with my friend Mary Ellen...

195
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:25,490
...who couldn't be here tonight, because... It's not...

196
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:28,290
It's not important. Well, she's in rehab.

197
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:33,670
Anyway. So Joey said that he was fixing me up with his friend Mike...

198
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:38,050
...only he didn't have a friend Mike, so he just brought my Mike. And... And...

199
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,880
Then...

200
00:10:40,050 --> 00:10:43,390
But despite, you know... It got good.

201
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:48,850
I wanna take a moment to mention my mother, who couldn't be here.

202
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:50,730
Oh, God.

203
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:53,150
And... And moment's over.

204
00:10:53,310 --> 00:10:56,320
So okay... Oh, no, forget that.

205
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,570
I can forget that. Oh, this is funny.

206
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:02,240
Oh, but you need to know that to get that.

207
00:11:02,450 --> 00:11:05,080
So... Oh, well, okay.

208
00:11:05,330 --> 00:11:07,490
I... Okay.

209
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:10,660
Okay, Monica, I can't do it like this!

210
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:15,500
This is my wedding, okay? I don't want this...

211
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:18,170
Or this... Or this...

212
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,590
Okay? I just wanted a simple wedding...

213
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:24,050
...where my fiancé can go to the bathroom any time he wants!

214
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,020
You know what? You're done.

215
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,020
What?

216
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:32,020
You're fired!

217
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:34,900
Cheers.

218
00:11:44,490 --> 00:11:47,120
Hey.

219
00:11:44,490 --> 00:11:47,120
Happy wedding day.

220
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,950
Happy my wedding day to you.

221
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:52,460
Joey, listen, this is gonna be bridesmaid central, all right?

222
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:55,000
We're gonna have hair and makeup in the bathroom.

223
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:58,750
I had to move a couple things in the fridge to make room for the corsages.

224
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:02,470
Man! I wouldn't have had breakfast if I knew there was gonna be corsages.

225
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,300
Hi.

226
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:11,470
About last night...

227
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:14,310
I know you're under a lot of stress, and...

228
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:18,650
Well, even though the things you said hurt me a little bit...

229
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,940
My point is...

230
00:12:22,110 --> 00:12:24,650
Well, I'm willing to take my job back.

231
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:28,120
Oh, well, that's okay.

232
00:12:29,030 --> 00:12:33,330
I think you and I will do much better if you're just here as a bridesmaid.

233
00:12:34,330 --> 00:12:37,210
Oh, is that so?

234
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:38,710
Okay.

235
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:41,340
If that's really what you want, then here.

236
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:44,670
I give you the headset. I don't really wanna give you the headset.

237
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:50,390
I guess if you're taking over, then you should probably return these messages.

238
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,810
This is a lot.

239
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,810
Uh-huh.

240
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,850
But I'm sure you can handle this. I have won awards...

241
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:59,190
...for my organizational skills. But I'm sure you'll do fine.

242
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,780
You've won awards?

243
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,780
I printed them out on my computer.

244
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,200
Hey.

245
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,200
Hi.

246
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:08,320
Where's Rach?

247
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:08,320
She's in her room. Why?

248
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:11,030
I have to talk to her about this groomsman situation.

249
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:14,870
I'm not gonna watch Chandler up there while I'm in the seats like some chump.

250
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:23,090
My God, you're breathtaking.

251
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:27,550
What do you want?

252
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:31,680
You haven't by any chance chosen a groomsman yet, have you?

253
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:34,520
Ross, please don't make this harder than it already is.

254
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,560
I'm not. I'm making it easier. Pick me.

255
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:41,900
Chandler said it's important to him too.

256
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:41,900
Listen. Listen.

257
00:13:42,230 --> 00:13:45,860
Whoever you pick is gonna walk down the aisle with you.

258
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:49,570
Now, I promise I won't say a word. But if you pick Chandler...

259
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:53,330
...he's gonna be whispering stupid jokes in your ear the whole time.

260
